<title>DENMARK: 2nd Danish, Swedish beet tests show mixed yields.</title>
<headline>2nd Danish, Swedish beet tests show mixed yields.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Denmark's second beet tests on September 2, issued by sole producer Danisco A/S on Thursday, showed 6.18 tonnes of sugar per hectare vs 6.92 percent average over the past five years with sugar content at 15.7 percent (15.4).</p>
<p>Figures for Sweden were 5.95 percent (6.46) tonnes/hectare and sugar content 15.7 percent (15.6).</p>
<p>DENMARK			2nd test 96   2nd test 95  1st test 96</p>
<p>Tonnes beet per hectare     39.3	   40.8	   26.4</p>
<p>Percent sugar in beet	 15.7	   16.0	   15.7</p>
<p>Tonnes sugar per hectare    6.18	   6.52	   4.13</p>
<p>SWEDEN</p>
<p>Tonnes beet per hectare     38.0	   38.5	    22.1</p>
<p>Percent sugar in beet	 15.7	   17.1	    15.8</p>
<p>Tonnes sugar per hectare    5.95	   6.59	    3.50</p>
</text>
